# Vendored: Utonia Point Transformer V3

Source: https://github.com/Pointcept/Utonia, commit `9a13cbfe8d018ac0483abaee6992fee0e4f07b85`. Licence: Apache-2.0 (`LICENSE` here;
file headers: Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates; "Pointcept detached version", Xiaoyang Wu).

Files are unmodified copies of `utonia/{model,module,structure,utils}.py` and `utonia/serialization/*.py`; `__init__.py` is an empty file (the upstream one imports the whole package).
Used only as a randomly initialised, encoder-only backbone (`enc_mode=True`); the pretrained weights are never loaded.
It needs `spconv`, `cumm`, `torch_scatter`, `timm`, `addict`, `huggingface_hub` and `packaging` (the upstream file imports them at the top).

This is not the original PTv3 (Pointcept/PointTransformerV3): it adds 3D rotary position encoding on queries and keys, optional layer scale and grid pooling and unpooling in place of serialized pooling, and has no PDNorm.

